+# GOAL — block 14: the formation-rate clause witness — no covariant clock law reaches the static law on a plaquette; every one does on a tree (2026-09-15)
+
+**Owner directive (2026-09-15):** don't stop; when a lane is exhausted, step back, assess the next lane and take it; no subagents; derivations over computation.
+
+**Why this block.** The derivation campaign's verdict table (#8093) lists "formation rate" as *to compute*: exhibit two covariant rate laws whose induced order laws give different finished-window laws, and record the separating clause candidates — (a) a rate independent of the nearest-neighbour conditions, (b) a rate determined by them, (c) no clause (registered data). No PR and no note on `main` (`f1755b6e10`) does it. The census note on `main` (2026-09-13) supplies the multiset key (Lemma L) and the uniform mixture's distance to the static law; block 01 (on `main`) supplies Theorem B (equality of the two readings when every record forms with at most one recorded neighbour). The block goes one step past the witness: it asks whether *any* covariant rate law can make the formation reading reproduce the static law — the reconciliation the repository's static reconstruction would need — and answers it exactly.
+
+**Object.** A finite window `Λ ⊂ Z³`; the six-axis menu with the product rule `(p, q, r)`, executed at `(3, 1, 2)`; records form one at a time; each unrecorded site `x` carries an exponential clock of rate `λ(x, S, v_S) ≥ 0` depending covariantly (lattice translations and proper cubic rotations acting on sites and values together) on the current recorded set `S` and its values; clocks are independent and memoryless; when `x`'s clock rings first, `x` records a value drawn from the rule given its recorded neighbours. *Value-blind* laws depend on `S` only; the three executed ones: uniform (`λ ≡ 1`), seeded (`λ = 1` if `x` has a recorded neighbour or `S = ∅`, else `0`), attracting (`λ = 1 + k`, `k` the number of recorded neighbours). One value-dependent law: parallel growth (`λ = 1 + [some recorded neighbour's value is the axis pointing from it to x]`).
+
+**Contract.**
+- R1 (clocks to orders): the next site is `x` with probability `λ_x/Σλ`, independent of the waiting time; the finished law is the jump chain's; for value-blind laws it is the mixture `Σ_σ P_R(σ) μ_σ` and depends on `R` only through the induced distribution on recorded-set multisets (Lemma L).
+- R2 (the witness): on `2×3` the three value-blind laws give pairwise different finished laws (exact total variations; the uniform one reproduces the census note's Theorem 3 rational); on the `2×2×2` cube the all-`+x` probability differs; the parallel-growth law differs from all three on the plaquette.
+- R3 (trees): on every tree window the seeded law gives the static law exactly (each record after the first has exactly one recorded neighbour; Theorem B); executed on the path and the star; the uniform law does not.
+- R4 (the plaquette no-go): for **every** covariant rate law — arbitrary causal dependence on the recorded values included — the finished law of the `2×2` plaquette is not the static law at every non-constant rule. Proof: the first site is uniform; from `S = {s}` the probability of the diagonal candidate depends only on the type of `v_s` (toward / away from the diagonal / perpendicular); for patterns whose two diagonals have the same pair type, `μ/Π_edges K = (1/4) Σ_s G(p_{type(s)}, d)` with `G(p, d) = (1 − p) d/6 + p d²/36` strictly increasing in `d = 1/K_2`; the patterns `(+x, −x, +x, −x)` and `(+x, +x, −x, −x)` have the same type multiset and `d_same ≠ d_anti` when `p ≠ q`; `(+x, −x, +y, +y)` gives `d_orth` when `p = q ≠ r`.
+- R5 (corollary): the static plaquette law is not a convex combination of the order laws.
+- R6 (executed): the parallel-growth law's plaquette law lies outside the affine span of the order laws.
+- The clause candidates recorded, not adopted; the owner's decision named.
+- N-gate for R4–R5.
+
+**Lens pass (self-run panel, before the primary).**
+- *"The witness is a corollary of order dependence (#8137) and the multiset key."* The witness alone, yes. R4 is not: it quantifies over every covariant rate law, value-dependent ones included, and uses the plaquette's symmetry types; R3 is the positive half (trees). Together they say exactly where a rate clause can and cannot deliver the static reading.
+- *"Value-dependent rates could bias the order to compensate."* Handled: the first site is uniform by the 90° rotation; the diagonal probability from `{s}` depends only on the type of `v_s` by the 180° rotation about the diagonal axis; in the path class the closing diagonal is irrelevant when both diagonals have the same type; the comparison patterns have equal type multisets.
+- *"Only one window."* The no-go is stated for the plaquette only; larger windows are not claimed (their class structure differs). The plaquette suffices for the clause table.
+- *"Rates that depend on the window?"* The rate law is a lattice function of `(x, S, v_S)`; the window only sets which sites can form; covariance is under the lattice group.
+
+**Forbidden phrases (beyond the lane's standing list):** "selects the physical rate", "the rate clause is adopted", "converge", "emergent", "certified".
+
+**Prior-art search at `origin/main` `f1755b6e10`.** `git grep -l -iE "random.priority|exponential clock|rate law|formation rate"` → the census note (uniform mixture), gravity/native notes using "rate" in other senses; no rate-law witness, no reachability statement. Open PRs: none on the rate seam (#8137 order dependence; #8140–#8145 finite-clock lanes; #8146/#8147 this lane).
